$ jailops host firewall show
ACTION   DIR   PROTO         PORTS   FROM   WHAT
pass     in    -             -       any    loopback (lo0 is not filtered) (always)
pass     in    -             -       any    the jails' own anchors (jailops/*) come first (always)
block    in    -             -       any    everything not passed below (always)
pass     out   -             -       any    everything the host sends, and the replies to it (always)
pass     in    icmp6         -       any    neighbour discovery and router advertisements (always)
pass     in    icmp, icmp6   -       any    path MTU discovery and ICMP errors (always)
pass     in    tcp           22      any    ssh
pass     in    tcp           39110   any    JailOps console and API
pass     in    icmp, icmp6   -       any    ping (echo requests)

Managed:     yes (module firewall)
Template:    default
pf:          running
pf.conf:     the administrator's
Warning:     ssh is open to the world: narrow ssh allow_from to the addresses you administer from

$ jailops --dry-run host firewall set --ssh-from 192.0.2.0/24 --ssh-from 2001:db8:a::/48 --confirm-within 5m
--- /etc/pf.conf
+++ /etc/pf.conf
-(the administrator's own pf.conf)
+pass in from any  # loopback (lo0 is not filtered)
+pass in from any  # the jails' own anchors (jailops/*) come first
+block in from any  # everything not passed below
+pass out from any  # everything the host sends, and the replies to it
+pass in icmp6 from any  # neighbour discovery and router advertisements
+pass in icmp, icmp6 from any  # path MTU discovery and ICMP errors
+pass in tcp 22 from 192.0.2.0/24, 2001:db8:a::/48  # ssh
+pass in tcp 39110 from any  # JailOps console and API
+pass in icmp, icmp6 from any  # ping (echo requests)
dry-run: would
  check the rendered file with pfctl -n
  write /etc/pf.conf
  pfctl -f /etc/pf.conf
  revert in 300 seconds unless confirmed

$ jailops host firewall set --ssh-port 0
! invalid: ssh port 0 is not a port (1-65535)
[exit 2]

$ jailops host firewall set --allow tcp 80 comment web
! invalid: allow rows need the template custom-rules, not default
! hint: set template to custom-rules, or leave allow out
[exit 2]

$ jailops host firewall set --template custom-rules --allow tcp
! usage: --allow is "PROTO PORTS [from SOURCE,...] [comment TEXT]", for example "tcp 80,443 from 192.0.2.0/24 comment web", not "tcp"
! hint: run 'jailops host firewall set --help' for usage
[exit 2]

$ jailops host firewall set --confirm-within 5
! usage: --confirm-within is 10 to 1800 seconds, not "5"
! hint: run 'jailops host firewall set --help' for usage
[exit 2]

$ jailops host firewall set --icmp sometimes
! usage: --icmp is enable or disable, not "sometimes"
! hint: run 'jailops host firewall set --help' for usage
[exit 2]

$ jailops host firewall set --template custom-rules --set admins=192.0.2.0/24,2001:db8:a::/48 --ssh-from @admins --allow tcp 80,443 comment web --allow udp 51820 from 2001:db8:1::/56 --confirm-within 90s
--- /etc/pf.conf
+++ /etc/pf.conf
-(the administrator's own pf.conf)
+pass in from any  # loopback (lo0 is not filtered)
+pass in from any  # the jails' own anchors (jailops/*) come first
+block in from any  # everything not passed below
+pass out from any  # everything the host sends, and the replies to it
+pass in icmp6 from any  # neighbour discovery and router advertisements
+pass in icmp, icmp6 from any  # path MTU discovery and ICMP errors
+pass in tcp 22 from @admins  # ssh
+pass in tcp 39110 from any  # JailOps console and API
+pass in tcp 80, 443 from any  # web
+pass in udp 51820 from 2001:db8:1::/56
+pass in icmp, icmp6 from any  # ping (echo requests)
  check the rendered file with pfctl -n
  write /etc/pf.conf
  pfctl -f /etc/pf.conf
  revert in 90 seconds unless confirmed
host firewall: applied; it REVERTS at 09:01:30Z (in 90 s) unless you confirm it: jailops host confirm --id 00000000f00d0001

