$ jailops host firewall diff
host firewall: /etc/pf.conf is what JailOps would write

$ jailops host firewall apply -f <dir>/fw.yaml --confirm-within 120
--- /etc/pf.conf
+++ /etc/pf.conf
-pass in from any  # loopback (lo0 is not filtered)
-pass in from any  # the jails' own anchors (jailops/*) come first
-block in from any  # everything not passed below
-pass out from any  # everything the host sends, and the replies to it
-pass in icmp6 from any  # neighbour discovery and router advertisements
-pass in icmp, icmp6 from any  # path MTU discovery and ICMP errors
-pass in tcp 22 from @admins  # ssh
-pass in tcp 39110 from any  # JailOps console and API
-pass in tcp 80, 443 from any  # web
-pass in udp 51820 from 2001:db8:1::/56
-pass in icmp, icmp6 from any  # ping (echo requests)
+pass in from any  # loopback (lo0 is not filtered)
+pass in from any  # the jails' own anchors (jailops/*) come first
+pass in from any  # everything (open template)
+pass out from any  # everything the host sends, and the replies to it
+pass in icmp6 from any  # neighbour discovery and router advertisements
+pass in icmp, icmp6 from any  # path MTU discovery and ICMP errors
  check the rendered file with pfctl -n
  write /etc/pf.conf
  pfctl -f /etc/pf.conf
  revert in 120 seconds unless confirmed
warning: ssh is open to the world: narrow ssh allow_from to the addresses you administer from
warning: the open template passes everything to the host; use it only behind another firewall
host firewall: applied; it REVERTS at 09:02:00Z (in 120 s) unless you confirm it: jailops host confirm --id 00000000f00d0002

